{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["And these are the generations of Aharon and Moshe — first he counted the generations of Yisra'el, then the generations of the priests, then the generations of the Levites. And now he counts the generations of Aharon and the generations of Moshe before us together with the Levites, as it is written: ״ולקהת משפחת העמרמי״ — this is Moshe (and Aharon and his sons who are reckoned over the tribe of Levi, for Amram had no sons other than Moshe and Aharon): ״ויבדל אהרן להקדישו״ — and Moshe and his sons are reckoned over the tribe of Levi." "On the day that YHWH spoke with Moshe on Mount Sinai — for this is before the Mishkan was set up; then they were four, but in the second year when the Mishkan was set up in the wilderness of Sinai they did not remain, for El'azar and Itamar, as I explained above at the beginning of the pericope. For every place where it says 'on Mount Sinai' — this is before the Mishkan was set up; but once the Tent of Meeting was built, it says only: 'in the wilderness of Sinai.'"], :book :numbers, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "The parenthetical structure and the dangling phrase 'ויבדל אהרן להקדישו' appear to introduce a lemma (from v. 3) whose comment is compressed or possibly truncated in the witness; rendered hyper-literally as it stands."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:49:43.720744034Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}